          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "MW explains mūla as probably \"firmly fixed\", but CDIAL 10250 thinks its sound variation points to a non-Aryan, perhaps Dravidian, origin, so the question is not settled. Hindi mūlī, \"radish\", the root vegetable, comes from it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What holds the tree down."
